WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:05.680
Obi-Wan Kenobi is one of the most iconic&nbsp;
characters in the Star Wars universe. But&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.680 --> 00:00:09.840
who knew he owes his origins to a&nbsp;
certain late night talk show host?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:09.840 --> 00:00:13.760
Keep watching to discover the&nbsp;
untold truth of Obi-Wan Kenobi.

00:00:14.640 --> 00:00:18.960
Fans are often divided by George Lucas's&nbsp;
late-career contributions to the Star&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:18.960 --> 00:00:23.200
Wars franchise. In some ways, it&nbsp;
can feel like he's both the best&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:23.200 --> 00:00:27.360
and worst thing to ever happen to the&nbsp;
saga, and, for a long time, at least,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:32.400
whatever Lucas said about his universe would&nbsp;
quickly become law — even if he was joking.

00:00:32.400 --> 00:00:38.160
At the Star Wars Celebration V in 2010,&nbsp;
Lucas was being interviewed by Jon Stewart,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.160 --> 00:00:43.040
who observed that, while we know about the home&nbsp;
worlds of most of the saga's main characters,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.040 --> 00:00:49.520
Obi-Wan Kenobi's is a mystery. So he posed the&nbsp;
question: just where does Obi-Wan hail from?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.520 --> 00:00:55.280
At this point, Lucas paused to think, spurring&nbsp;
Stewart to insist that he not just make up his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:55.280 --> 00:01:01.280
answer. Lucas sarcastically shot back that he'd&nbsp;
never make something like this up, then proclaimed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:01.280 --> 00:01:07.840
that Obi-Wan's home world is the planet of Stewjon&nbsp;
— an obvious amalgamation of Jon Stewart's name.

00:01:07.840 --> 00:01:13.360
While this was obviously an off-hand joke for&nbsp;
Lucas, the nature of Lucas' influence on Star Wars&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:13.360 --> 00:01:19.040
means it's now enshrined in canon. If you visit&nbsp;
Obi-Wan's page on the official Star Wars site,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:19.040 --> 00:01:23.920
you'll even find that Stewjon is listed&nbsp;
as his homeworld on his databank profile.

00:01:25.120 --> 00:01:29.600
In the Star Wars universe, there's something to&nbsp;
be said about the bond between a padawan and a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:29.600 --> 00:01:33.760
master. As Jedi are instructed to forsake&nbsp;
their emotional ties and relationships,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:33.760 --> 00:01:38.160
a padawan's closest familial bond&nbsp;
becomes the one who instructs them&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:38.160 --> 00:01:42.400
in the ways of the force. As a result,&nbsp;
there's a kind of lineage that can be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:42.400 --> 00:01:47.120
spoken of in the ranks of the Jedi — one&nbsp;
that transcends genetic relationships.

00:01:47.120 --> 00:01:49.280
"Why do I get the feeling you're&nbsp;
going to be the death of me?"

00:01:49.840 --> 00:01:53.840
"Don't say that, Master. You're the&nbsp;
closest thing I have to a father."

00:01:54.400 --> 00:01:59.680
Obi-Wan Kenobi is, perhaps, the most pivotal&nbsp;
and influential Jedi Master in Star Wars.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:00.240 --> 00:02:04.880
Not only did he train the greatest Sith Lord&nbsp;
in the galaxy, his own skills and training&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:04.880 --> 00:02:10.240
can be traced back to the ancient era of the High&nbsp;
Republic. During this time, the thriving Republic&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:10.240 --> 00:02:15.200
was expanding to the outer territories within&nbsp;
the galaxy and the Jedi were at their very peak.

00:02:15.200 --> 00:02:21.040
How does this work? Well, in The Empire Strikes&nbsp;
Back, it's implied that Yoda trained Obi-Wan. But&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:21.040 --> 00:02:26.320
the prequel trilogy makes it quite clear that the&nbsp;
bulk of his training came from Qui-Gon Jinn. It's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:26.320 --> 00:02:31.520
later revealed, however, that Jinn was trained by&nbsp;
Count Dooku , who was, in turn, trained by Yoda.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:31.520 --> 00:02:36.720
So no matter how you spin it, Obi-Wan's skills&nbsp;
are derived from Yoda's, and Yoda learned his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:36.720 --> 00:02:42.320
powers as a padawan nearly a millennium prior,&nbsp;
during the High Republic era. It's one heck of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:42.320 --> 00:02:47.120
a long line — and one that stretches not just&nbsp;
into the past, but far into the future, too.

00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:53.040
Obi-Wan's journey from the Galactic Republic to&nbsp;
the Galactic Empire is driven by his incessant&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:53.040 --> 00:02:57.200
need to do the right thing and live by&nbsp;
the Jedi code. In the prequel films,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:57.200 --> 00:03:01.360
he often appears to harp on Anakin for&nbsp;
acting outside the tenets of the Jedi,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:01.360 --> 00:03:04.800
and he rarely wavers in his&nbsp;
loyalties to the Jedi Council.

00:03:04.800 --> 00:03:09.840
There is, however, one notable exception&nbsp;
to this. Sadly, only one film in the saga&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:09.840 --> 00:03:14.960
portrays the relationship between Obi-Wan and his&nbsp;
master Qui-Gon Jinn, but it's a fascinating one&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:14.960 --> 00:03:19.920
nonetheless. Throughout The Phantom Menace,&nbsp;
Obi-Wan objects to his master's decision&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:19.920 --> 00:03:24.320
to bring Anakin Skywalker into the Jedi&nbsp;
fold — but he supports Qui-Gon regardless.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:24.880 --> 00:03:29.200
Qui-Gon, meanwhile, constantly challenges&nbsp;
the council and is clearly unwilling to fall&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:29.200 --> 00:03:34.400
in line behind their agenda, especially when&nbsp;
they deny his request to have Anakin trained.

00:03:34.400 --> 00:03:38.960
Sticking to his convictions, Qui-Gon commits&nbsp;
to teaching Anakin. In his dying breath,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:38.960 --> 00:03:45.120
Qui-Gon asks Obi-Wan to train Anakin, insisting&nbsp;
he is the chosen one. Risking his standing among&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:45.120 --> 00:03:50.000
the Jedi Council, Obi-Wan remains loyal to his&nbsp;
dying master's request and assumes mentorship&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:50.000 --> 00:03:54.640
over the young padawan. Despite his own&nbsp;
feelings and the Council's original decision,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:54.640 --> 00:04:01.040
Obi-Wan's loyalty to Qui-Gon Jinn clearly runs&nbsp;
far deeper than his own commitment to the Jedi.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:01.040 --> 00:04:04.720
At one point, he even tells Yoda that&nbsp;
he'll go against the council's wishes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:04.720 --> 00:04:08.880
if he doesn't have their support — just&nbsp;
like Qui-Gon. It's a stirring testament&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:08.880 --> 00:04:13.743
to the incredibly close relationship&nbsp;
between Obi-Wan and his former master.

00:04:13.760 --> 00:04:17.040
Jedi Knights are known for their&nbsp;
prowess in the use of the Force,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:17.040 --> 00:04:22.240
and Obi-Wan Kenobi became a legend among them&nbsp;
by defeating Darth Maul in The Phantom Menace.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:22.240 --> 00:04:25.760
Of course, Darth Maul would return to&nbsp;
skulk in the shadows for years to come,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:25.760 --> 00:04:30.400
but as far as the prequels go, their&nbsp;
battle is as important as it is dramatic.

00:04:30.400 --> 00:04:35.520
At the time of their duel, a Sith Lord had&nbsp;
not been seen in nearly a thousand years.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:35.520 --> 00:04:39.840
Defeating — and seemingly killing — one&nbsp;
solidified Obi-Wan's position among the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:39.840 --> 00:04:44.960
top ranks of the Jedi, and he was granted the&nbsp;
rank of Jedi Knight for accomplishing this feat.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:44.960 --> 00:04:49.440
The Sith are capable and dangerous foes to a&nbsp;
Jedi for a reason, as they're less constrained&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:49.440 --> 00:04:54.240
by the moral platitudes of the Jedi Order.&nbsp;
Simply put, defeating a Sith Lord is no mean&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:54.240 --> 00:04:59.760
feat even for a Jedi Master. Obi-Wan's victory&nbsp;
over Darth Maul, given his relative youth and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:59.760 --> 00:05:04.840
inexperience, is one of his greatest and&nbsp;
most under-appreciated accomplishments.

00:05:05.840 --> 00:05:10.400
While the duel between Obi-Wan and Darth&nbsp;
Maul marks the climax of The Phantom Menace,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:10.400 --> 00:05:15.200
the two would be destined for many more&nbsp;
rounds via the franchise's animated shows.

00:05:15.760 --> 00:05:20.640
On at least three occasions in The Clone&nbsp;
Wars and Rebels, Obi-Wan and Darth Maul have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:20.640 --> 00:05:24.880
been reunited in combat. It's soon revealed&nbsp;
that Darth Maul's connection with the Force,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:24.880 --> 00:05:30.640
as well as his intense hatred for Obi-Wan, kept&nbsp;
him alive after being severed in two; eventually,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:30.640 --> 00:05:35.840
he obtained robotic legs that enabled him to&nbsp;
once again operate like normal. However, he grew&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:35.840 --> 00:05:41.040
resentful towards the Jedi for taking away his&nbsp;
future at Palpatine's side. Maul's brother Savage&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:41.040 --> 00:05:46.720
Opress soon located him, and the two set off on&nbsp;
their own path toward building a criminal empire.

00:05:47.280 --> 00:05:51.600
Ultimately, just prior to the events of A&nbsp;
New Hope, Darth Maul discovers that Obi-Wan&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:51.600 --> 00:05:57.360
is hiding on Tatooine and deduces that he must be&nbsp;
serving a purpose there — or protecting somebody.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:57.360 --> 00:06:02.320
He hunts down his old enemy, but, after a brief&nbsp;
clash, Obi-Wan delivers him a fatal wound. In&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:02.320 --> 00:06:08.640
Maul's dying breath, he asks Obi-Wan if the one he&nbsp;
protects is the chosen one. Obi-Wan confirms this,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:08.640 --> 00:06:12.480
and Maul dies believing that this&nbsp;
chosen one will avenge them both.

00:06:12.480 --> 00:06:16.960
Clearly, Maul always knew the Sith were his&nbsp;
true enemies, having stolen him as a child&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:16.960 --> 00:06:22.000
and indoctrinated him in the ways of the&nbsp;
dark side. And while Luke Skywalker didn't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:22.000 --> 00:06:26.320
avenge Maul in quite the way he might have&nbsp;
thought, Obi-Wan's mission to protect and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:26.320 --> 00:06:30.920
train the young Jedi nevertheless delivered&nbsp;
justice for the embittered ex-Sith Lord.

00:06:31.920 --> 00:06:37.520
The Jedi Ahsoka is known for many things, one&nbsp;
being that she was the only Jedi apprentice of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:37.520 --> 00:06:43.280
Anakin Skywalker prior to his turn to the dark&nbsp;
side of the Force. Her quest to becoming a Jedi&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:43.280 --> 00:06:48.000
begins in The Clone Wars animated series, as&nbsp;
Anakin trains the young padawan into becoming&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:48.000 --> 00:06:53.600
a fully-fledged Jedi Knight. Most of the time,&nbsp;
Obi-Wan, Anakin, and Ahsoka operate together&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:53.600 --> 00:06:59.280
on missions, and Obi-Wan is typically on-hand to&nbsp;
aid Anakin in his efforts to train his apprentice.

00:07:00.080 --> 00:07:04.640
Likewise, Ahsoka recognizes Obi-Wan's status&nbsp;
in the Jedi Order, often going directly to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:04.640 --> 00:07:10.160
him to seek guidance, and the two forge a&nbsp;
unique bond. Tragically, following Order 66,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:10.160 --> 00:07:15.920
Ahsoka and Obi-Wan never make contact again, as&nbsp;
they're both forced into hiding from the Empire.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:15.920 --> 00:07:19.829
It's quite likely that he never even knew&nbsp;
that she survived the purging of the Jedi .

00:07:21.360 --> 00:07:26.480
While Obi-Wan may be a legendary Jedi Knight,&nbsp;
he isn't infallible. Most of his shortcomings&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:26.480 --> 00:07:32.160
are due to the rigid traditions of the Jedi Order&nbsp;
that Obi-Wan adheres to with precision. Indeed,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:32.160 --> 00:07:36.160
perhaps his most destructive flaw is&nbsp;
his aversion to matters of the heart.

00:07:36.160 --> 00:07:40.160
The Jedi have always denied their emotions&nbsp;
and romantic attachments to others,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:40.160 --> 00:07:45.440
but this makes them more susceptible to&nbsp;
volatility and instability. The result? This.

00:07:51.520 --> 00:07:56.640
Obi-Wan is particularly adherent to this rule,&nbsp;
and it even prevents him from discussing his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:56.640 --> 00:08:01.200
padawan's obvious attraction to Padme. Had&nbsp;
this been an open topic for discussion,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:01.200 --> 00:08:04.960
perhaps Obi-Wan could have circumvented&nbsp;
Palpatine's efforts and reasoned with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:04.960 --> 00:08:09.600
Anakin before tragedy struck. Likewise, his&nbsp;
fear of impacting the fate of the galaxy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:09.600 --> 00:08:14.800
by bringing up family drama prevents him from&nbsp;
telling Luke the identity of his real father.

00:08:14.800 --> 00:08:19.120
In Return of the Jedi, Obi-Wan counsels&nbsp;
Luke to kill his father — a task Luke&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:19.120 --> 00:08:23.680
doesn't think he can perform. Obi-Wan then&nbsp;
laments a failure that hadn't even occurred.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:24.240 --> 00:08:28.240
Of course, Luke's love for his father later&nbsp;
brings about the downfall of the Empire,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:28.240 --> 00:08:32.080
proving that the Jedi, and Obi-Wan&nbsp;
himself, were very much in the wrong.

00:08:33.040 --> 00:08:39.440
In a 2015 run of Star Wars comics published by&nbsp;
Marvel, Luke discovers Obi-Wan's old journals.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:39.440 --> 00:08:44.560
Issue #7, written by Jason Aaron, details&nbsp;
an adventure in which he rescued Luke from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:44.560 --> 00:08:49.040
Jabba's enforcers as a young boy. At the&nbsp;
time, Luke had become angered by Jabba's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:49.040 --> 00:08:54.320
henchmen collecting "water" tax from the moisture&nbsp;
farms. After attempting to steal the water back,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:54.320 --> 00:08:58.000
Luke was caught, and came very&nbsp;
close to being sold into slavery.

00:08:58.560 --> 00:09:03.280
Luckily for the intrepid little do-gooder,&nbsp;
old Ben Kenobi had been watching his back&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:03.280 --> 00:09:08.800
from the shadows. Obi-Wan leapt into action,&nbsp;
using the Force to dispatch Luke's captors.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:08.800 --> 00:09:12.880
The next morning, Luke awakened to&nbsp;
Aunt Beru asking him what had happened;&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:12.880 --> 00:09:14.960
he stated that he simply could not remember.

00:09:15.680 --> 00:09:20.400
This would seem to imply that Ben Kenobi used&nbsp;
the Force to wipe Luke's memory of the event.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:20.400 --> 00:09:24.400
True to his word and purpose, this wasn't&nbsp;
the only time that Obi-Wan has demonstrated&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:24.400 --> 00:09:29.440
his watchful eye and protective actions over&nbsp;
Luke. The most famous of these, of course,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:29.440 --> 00:09:34.480
occurs in live action when he scares away the&nbsp;
Tusken Raiders in A New Hope — and there can be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:34.480 --> 00:09:40.000
little doubt that he'll get the chance again&nbsp;
when Obi-Wan Kenobi airs on Disney+ in 2022.

00:09:40.880 --> 00:09:45.120
Building an evolving story that grows both&nbsp;
backwards and forward can be extremely&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:45.120 --> 00:09:50.160
difficult work. For George Lucas, modernizing&nbsp;
old plot points eventually became a tug of war&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:50.160 --> 00:09:55.520
with simply telling solid stories — leading to&nbsp;
some substantial plot holes in his franchise.

00:09:55.520 --> 00:10:01.120
One such trouble spot comes from Obi-Wan&nbsp;
apparently having forgotten R2-D2 and C-3PO&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:01.120 --> 00:10:05.600
from his days as a young Jedi Knight, despite&nbsp;
all the adventures they shared together.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:05.600 --> 00:10:10.080
When Alec Guinness sees the droids in A&nbsp;
New Hope, he barely even acknowledges them.

00:10:10.080 --> 00:10:11.920
"Well then, the droid does belong to you."

00:10:11.920 --> 00:10:14.640
"I don't seem to remember ever owning a droid."

00:10:14.640 --> 00:10:19.840
One fan theory argues that Obi-Wan may have&nbsp;
voluntarily erased any memory that connected&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:19.840 --> 00:10:23.760
him with dissidents of the Empire in&nbsp;
order to protect himself and Luke.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:23.760 --> 00:10:27.680
It's a nice idea, but nothing exists&nbsp;
in canon to support it, and, for now,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:27.680 --> 00:10:32.160
fans will have to assume that, in A New Hope,&nbsp;
old Ben Kenobi is simply showing his age.

00:10:32.960 --> 00:10:36.800
At first pass, it might seem odd&nbsp;
that Han and Leia named their son&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:36.800 --> 00:10:42.240
after the name Obi-Wan took in exile. After&nbsp;
all, Han barely knew Ben Kenobi. Sure,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:42.240 --> 00:10:46.480
the old man had tagged along with Luke aboard the&nbsp;
Millennium Falcon, but he died at the hands of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:46.480 --> 00:10:52.160
Darth Vader mere hours later, after the crew was&nbsp;
pulled aboard the Death Star. Obi-Wan engages in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:52.160 --> 00:10:57.280
few notable interactions with Solo, and even&nbsp;
Leia knew him primarily from his reputation.

00:10:57.280 --> 00:11:01.600
That said, both of them were aboard the Death&nbsp;
Star, and if not for Obi-Wan's diversion and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:01.600 --> 00:11:05.840
sacrifice, the whole group might have been&nbsp;
killed. Most likely, as the years went by,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:05.840 --> 00:11:10.160
Luke shared Obi-Wan's stories with his sister&nbsp;
and brother-in-law, perhaps suggesting that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:10.160 --> 00:11:14.720
Ben Kenobi had helped bring the two of them&nbsp;
together. Suddenly the name "Ben" makes a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:14.720 --> 00:11:18.800
little more sense for the child of Han and&nbsp;
Leia. It's just a shame what happened next.

